gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.label.4=AAL Stuck and how to resolve
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.1=AAL can "stuck" sometimes and this will prevent AAL to operate further.
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.2=It is necessary to confirm that AAL does not require all of the necessary items to continue recipe processing.
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.3=Before a recipe starts, AAL checks all Hatches and Buses to verify the recipe, but once the recipe is confirmed, it starts the recipe as long as the Fluids and the first Slice's items are sufficient, even if the items are not fully available.
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.4=Ok - seems I can run recipe. start processing.
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.5=If there are not enough items to process the recipe, AAL becomes "stuck" and will not operate until the required items are received.
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.6=No Item - stuck from here!
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.7=The machine does not operate and waits until the required item is added to the stuck slice.
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.8=Item added - resume processing.
gregtech.multiblock.aal.ponder.operation.text.4.9=You can check controller's WAILA to see which slice is on stuck.